# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL MANAGER  --  concrete models, not abstract roles
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The registry above names ROLES ("Local instruction model"). This maps each
# role onto specific Hugging Face models with their real footprints, so the
# app can tell a learner what would actually be downloaded and whether this
# machine can run it -- rather than gesturing at "a local model".
#
# Selected for a heterogeneous stack rather than a pool of interchangeable
# chatbots: a tiny router, a mid-size creator, a separate critic, and two
# embedding options at different resource points. Running the same model
# twice under different names buys diversity in name only.
